{quote}*to filter our the so-called Credit Score metrics that we can’t defend from reclassification perspective*{quote}

Gotcha makes sense, especially in Europe. We can definitely explore the metrics & remove some which would cause issues. Just wanted to clarify this initiative could be rolled out only some of the markets as e.g. for drivers in Europe we don’t have much issues with driver debt / cash-blocking in general as majority of the rides are done via in-app payment methods. The markets I would definitely roll this out will be NG, GH, KE, ZA, TZ, TN, TH, AZ, PY, SA where we do have issues with driver debt hence maybe this risk could be neglected in these countries? But yeah if we should remove some of the metrics monitored then there’s nothing we can do about it & I’ll update the model. Will be waiting for your confirmation on this.

{quote}*to update the T&Cs*{quote}

If possible we’d like to roll this out globally → to give more visibility to the drivers on cash rides in general. But again if this will cause issues legally then the countries who definitely need it are listed above ^^. I’ve also looped in DriverX & lifecycle team to put together comms to educate the drivers on ‘how to get bigger cash-blocking limit’, communication of roll-out could be also shared within that message probably? In terms of T&Cs , again, I’ll be waiting for your confirmation

{quote}One more question - how does this feature work in a fleet market where fleet is invoicing the passenger for the trip instead of a driver?{quote}

Fleet drivers will never get cash-blocked as they don’t have their individual balance. We are planning to build a fleet cash-blocking in Q4 such that if the whole fleet’s balance goes under a set threshold all drivers driving within the fleet would get cash-blocked. The ticket describing this is here [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-18573|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-18573|smart-link]

