{quote}Benefits of solving the problem, ideally with estimates.{quote}

We can replace current manual Fraud review/approval system with tooling based and auditable system. Being compliant with “4-eye-review for production” concept. The time-to-market of Fraud RnA was significantly improved with RnA module integration, but unfortunately it’s lacking key functionality to fully deliver.
There have been few incidents in last year where a rule without approval caused an incident.
Example: [2022-12-30 [Fraud] - A logic issue on a fraud rule caused Rides orders in Norway to be rejected|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/4244799663/2022-12-30+Fraud+-+A+logic+issue+on+a+fraud+rule+caused+Rides+orders+in+Norway+to+be+rejected]

{quote}The kind of help you are looking for.{quote}

We request the extra functionality to be implemented so it covers also use cases other than dynamic config.

{quote}Any deadline? What happens if we don’t meet it?{quote}

It’s a blocker to rollout the RnA functionality for Fraud rules. This means, there is no enforced 4-eye-review for Fraud rule modifications (there are 1000+ active rules). Our analysts have to continue using current manual method. We have rolled out this functionality 1 of ~50 Fraud checkpoints for POC evaluation. Lack of custom slack channel and proper list of approvers was identified as a blocker.

{quote}Criteria for considering the dependency as fulfilled.{quote}

If the main requirements are fulfilled, we are happy. We don’t care about the implementation (e.g. we can manually manage the list of approvers as along as we are able to define specific slack channel for the client ID).

