Hi [~accountid:6215e9d79cd4a70071de651c], thanks for the background information. Below my comments:

*BACKGROUND*

* this agreement was awarded following a public tender and the Code of Public Contracts applies;
* the agreement is valid until end of the year 2023 and was executed by the local entity;
* we signed an honour committement that we would comply with the agreement, particularly “caderno de encargos”;
* according to “caderno de encargos”, payment is depended on the presentation of invoice to be paid in 30 days;
* following Article 299b of the Code of Public Contracts 
1 - Within the scope of the execution of public contracts, *co-contractors are obliged to issue electronic invoices which*, without prejudice to the requirements of tax legislation, *must contain the following elements*, where applicable:
a) File and invoice identifiers;
b) Invoicing period;
c) I*nformation on the co-contractor*;
d) Information on the public contractor;
e) Information on the beneficiary entity, if different from the previous one;
f) Information on the fiscal representative of the co-contractor;
g) Contract reference;
h) Delivery conditions;
i) Payment instructions;
j) Information on adjustments and charges;
l) Information on invoice headings;
m) Invoice totals.
* additionally Bolt has agreed to provide a *monthly account statement*.

*QUESTION*

Could we elaborate a document as an attachment to the contract contemplating our legal entities and that Bolt Ops OU (NIF: 980...) will be the supplier issuing the invoice, that Bolt SS, PT is the "representante fiscal"? 

* That would appear not possible since in this case we are in the context of a public tender. I would therefore propose Academia Militar the assignment of the contractual position of Bolt PT in the agreement to Bolt Operations OU and enquire what are the documents that would be required to be presented by Bolt Operations OU for such purpose. 
* This proposal is depended on the acceptance by Academia Militar and the ability of Bolt Operations to present the required documentation. According to clause 10 of the agreement: _10(5) The Second Party may not assign its contractual position or any of the rights and obligations arising from the contract without the authorization of the First Party;  10(6) For the purposes of the authorization provided for in the preceding paragraph, the assignee must submit all the qualification documents required of the assignor at the stage of formation of the contract in question._

Please let me know if you have any further questions and wish to discuss. Thank you.

