The process that I propose is the following:

# CS receives a request with a digital doc on Beehive;
# CS opens/decrypts the request with DigiDoc software and verifies it;
# If the doc is okay to go, CS forwards it to OPS;
# OPS digitally signs the doc and: 1) either sends it for CS to attach it to the ticket and send a final reply; 2) or sends the reply with a doc on Beehive themselves (for example, if the ticket is forwarded to Local OPS queue). It should stay in Beehive as Privacy wants us to document it there.

